WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.182
Read the recurrence
The initial term u zero is zero, and each new term is half the preceding term
plus three. We want a clear method for the formula and the limit.

2
00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:30.091
Find the fixed point
First look for the number that remains unchanged. Solve ell equal to half ell
plus three to obtain six. This is the fixed point.

3
00:00:30.091 --> 00:00:43.545
Obtain a geometric sequence
Set v n equal to u n minus six. Using the recurrence, each new term of v
becomes exactly half the preceding term.

4
00:00:43.545 --> 00:00:58.818
Return to u
The initial value v zero is minus six. Thus v n is minus six times one half to
the power n. Add six to return to u.

5
00:00:58.818 --> 00:01:14.545
Conclude
One half to the power n tends to zero, so u n tends to six. The formula also
shows that the sequence is increasing and remains below six.
